<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Tranquilidade boosts premiums.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Tranquilidade boosts premiums.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese insurance company Tranquilidade said consolidated premium income from direct insurance rose 29.1 percent to 98.4 billion escudos ($650 million) in the first 10 months of the year.</p>
<p>Life insurance rose 47.4 percent to 57.7 billion escudos, while non-life was up 9.9 percent at 40.7 billion.</p>
<p>($1=151.45 escudos)</p>
<p>-- Lisbon bureau 3511-3113121</p>
</text>
